      "authority_type": "opinion",
      "citation": "Madden v. Production Concrete, Inc., 2013-Ohio-5393",
      "text": "The elements of a claim of negligence are: (1) the existence of a legal duty owing from the defendant to the plaintiff; (2) the defendant's breach of that duty; and (3) injury to the plaintiff proximately resulting from such failure.",
